    {
      "id": "gassy_moo",
      "name": "Gassy Moo",
      "kind": "critter",
      "description": "A Moo eats 50 % of a plant’s maturity a cycle, which is two Gas Grass at 25 % each, and makes 10 kg/cycle of natural gas. Moos lay no eggs — they summon another by meteor roughly every 16 cycles — so there is no egg output either.\n\nWhich is why the grooming matters here for a different reason than anywhere else. Everywhere else grooming buys eggs; a Moo has none, so its grooming bought nothing at all in this app and was charged for anyway. What it actually buys is the metabolism: a tamed critter starts at -1 happiness and a glum one runs at a fifth, so an ungroomed Moo makes 2 kg of gas a cycle and not 10. The wiki puts it the other way round — its \"reproduction is tied closer to its critter metabolism\", so \"a satisfied gassy moo is just as effective as a happy gassy moo\". Satisfied is zero happiness, which is one point above glum: for a Moo, anything that gets it off the cliff is as good as a brushing.",
      "dupeLabourSecondsPerCycle": 12.0,
      "tags": [
